{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.GravitationalConstant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.GravitationalConstant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.gravitational_planck_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.gravitational_planck_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/gravitational-constant.lean#L63-L82","doc":"In Planck units, the gravitational constant is identically 1:\nG_Planck = G(q) · (ℏ_q / c_q)² = 1.\n\nThe hypothesis `_hu` pins `u` to the physical shift `q − 1`; the identity\nitself is the commutative-group cancellation `q²/u⁴ · u⁴/q² = 1` and so\nholds for any pair of units.  The old version needed `q > 1` only through\n`q ≠ 0`, `q ≠ 1`, which the unit hypotheses now carry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.gravitationalConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.gravitationalConstant","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/gravitational-constant.lean#L51-L61","doc":"**Gravitational constant** at substrate parameter q.\n\nG(q) := c_q³ · ℏ_q / S_cell(q)\n\nwhere c_q = 1/(q-1), ℏ_q = (q-1)/q, and S_cell = (q-1)²/q³. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:gravitational-constant","label":"def:gravitational-constant","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/gravitational-constant.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.cellEntropy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.cellEntropy","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/gravitational-constant.lean#L44-L49","doc":"Cumulative jet tower entropy: `S_cell(q) = (q − 1)² / q³`.\n\n`q u : Rˣ` are the substrate parameter and its shift `q − 1`, both as\nunits (§7c); `/` is division in the group `Rˣ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}